s the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(4) & =f(1,4)+f(3,4) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{20}+\\frac{1}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, $f(1,4)=\\frac{7}{20}.$ \n\nFinally, substituting  ${f}_{Y}(4)=\\frac{2}{5}$ and $f(1,4)=\\frac{7}{20}$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(1\\,|\\,4) & =P(X=1\\,|\\,Y=4) \\\\  & =\\frac{f(1,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{7}{20})}{(\\frac{2}{5})} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363288 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363289 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363288 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363290 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363288 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363291 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363288 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363292 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363288 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363293 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363288 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363288 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363288 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186363292 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363288 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a3c83bc5-8c9c-5ba3-9c2d-a22c540d169d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363289 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3}{10}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363289 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363289 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b23a91dd-7a01-54db-9c82-1cde58ce273a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363290 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{8}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363290 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363290 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8145968b-18ea-5743-b1bd-efc55f689163" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363291 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363291 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417]